     We:
       - Initialize diagonal to 1 and strict upper triangle to 0.
       - Compute only the upper triangle (i < j) via dot products.
       - Copy the upper triangle to the lower triangle at the end.
     This preserves the original semantics (diagonal forced to 1,
     symmetry enforced) while enabling straightforward parallelization. */

  /* Initialize diagonal and strict upper triangle. */
  for (i = 0; i < pb_m; i++)
